  "question": {
    "text": "Three lines are given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math><br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and<br /><math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#957;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#957;</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Let the lines cut the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at the points <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> respectively. If the area of the triangle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></math> then the value of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> equals_________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Finding point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8216;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8217;</mi></math><br />Line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and plane <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />General point of line <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> satisfy the plane<br /><math><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Hence, <math><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> ...(i)<br />For point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8216;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8217;</mi></math><br />General point of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Satisfy the plane and <math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Point <math><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> ...(ii)<br />Similarly for point <math><mi>&#8216;</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>&#8217;</mi></math><br />General point of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />Satisfy the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math><br />Point <math><mi>C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> ....(iii)<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math><br />Now area of triangle <math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>j</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8710;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math></p>",
